'>Heat Advisory</span></div><div class='icon' data-live='condition-icon'>☀️</div></div><div class='temp-row'><div class='temp' data-live='current-temp'>82°</div><div class='condition-col'><div class='condition' data-live='condition-text'>Clear & warm</div><div class='range'>H: <span data-live='today-high'>90°</span> L: <span data-live='today-low'>64°</span></div></div></div><div class='hourly' data-live='hourly-forecast'><div class='hour'><span class='hour-time'>8PM</span><span class='hour-icon'>☀️</span><span class='hour-temp'>82°</span></div><div class='hour'><span class='hour-time'>9PM</span><span class='hour-icon'>🌙</span><span class='hour-temp'>79°</span></div><div class='hour'><span class='hour-time'>10PM</span><span class='hour-icon'>🌙</span><span class='hour-temp'>77°</span></div><div class='hour'><span class='hour-time'>11PM</span><span class='hour-icon'>🌙</span><span class='hour-temp'>77°</span></div><div class='hour'><span class='hour-time'>12AM</span><span class='hour-icon'>🌙</span><span class='hour-temp'>73°</span></div><div class='hour'><span class='hour-time'>7:22PM</span><span class='hour-icon'>🌇</span><span class='hour-temp'>Sunset</span></div></div></body></html>"},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"weather","subtitle":null,"timestamp":"2026-03-20T02:36:17Z","title":"Menlo Park weather","type":"html-webview"}
{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_3499b675ea28cbd97d56d82fa30f46b2","createdAt":"2026-03-20T02:36:17Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-22T02:36:17Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_26e9691acd40f9067e364a194bc3415f","message":"While rivals pour tens of billions into AI infrastructure, Apple is monetizing through subscriptions and ecosystem stickiness — and it's working.","metadata":{"height":400,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}a.card-link{display:block;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}a.card-link:active{opacity:0.7}.hero-img{width:100%;height:clamp(120px,34vw,220px);object-fit:cover;display:block;background:var(--border)}.content{padding:16px 20px 20px}.headline{font-size:18px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--text)}.source{font-size:13px;color:var(--tertiary);font-weight:500;margin:0 0 10px}.summary{font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55;margin:0}</style></head><body><a class='card-link' href='https://www.alphapilot.tech/discover/apple-set-to-surpass-1-billion-in-ai-revenue-despite-late-market-entry' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'><img class='hero-img' src='https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1611532736597-de2d4265fba3?w=800&h=400&fit=crop' alt='Apple Park' onerror=\"this.style.display='none'\"><div class='content'><div class='headline'>Apple Quietly Hits $1B in AI Revenue</div><div class='source'>AlphaPilot Insights · Mar 19, 2026</div><div class='summary'>While Microsoft, Meta, and Google pour tens of billions into data centers and specialized AI chips, Apple is on track to pass $1 billion in AI-related revenue this year through premium subscriptions and AI-enhanced ecosystem features. Q1 2026 Services revenue hit $143.76B — up 15.6% year-over-year. The strategy: leverage 2 billion active devices rather than compete on raw model capability. The risk: falling too far behind on proprietary AI if third-party providers demand better terms.</div></div></a></body></html>","web_images":[{"image_url":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/news/apple-is-way-behind-in-aiand-still-making-a-20260318.jpg","source_url":"https://alphapilot.tech/discover/apple-set-to-surpass-1-billion-in-ai-revenue-despite-late-market-entry"}]},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"articles","subtitle":"AlphaPilot Insights · Mar 19, 2026","timestamp":"2026-03-20T02:36:17Z","title":"Apple Quietly Hits $1B in AI Revenue","type":"html-webview"}
{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_7bd4a4917fc8e113c9d6874ce5e404d8","createdAt":"2026-03-20T02:36:17Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-22T02:36:17Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_2fe826e6ba11c36638acc3b159a4a03c","message":"Meta confirmed dual-screen smart glasses for 2026, with a wrist controller and heads-up display on both lenses. Not full AR yet, but the platform your MRBD games will run on next.","metadata":{"height":340,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;padding:20px;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}h4{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 4px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3}.subtitle{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.4}.msg{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.5}.divider{border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:0}.point{padding:12px 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.4}.point strong{font-weight:600}.point-detail{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:2px 0 0}</style></head><body><h4>Meta's dual-display glasses ship this year</h4><div class='subtitle'>Your team's next hardware target is taking shape</div><p class='msg'>Meta confirmed dual-screen smart glasses for 2026 launch, with a wrist controller and heads-up display on both lenses. Not full AR yet — but the platform your MRBD games will likely run on next.</p><hr class='divider'><div class='point'><strong>Dual lens displays</strong><div class='point-detail'>Screens integrated into both lenses enable multitasking: navigation on one side, notifications on the other. Input via the neural-band wrist device.</div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='point'><strong>Stepping stone to full AR in 2027</strong><div class='point-detail'>The Display glasses sit between current Ray-Ban Meta and the Orion AR prototype. 2027 is when Meta targets a true spatial computing headset.</div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='point'><strong>What this means for MRBD</strong><div class='point-detail'>Dual displays could enable richer game UIs — HUD on one lens, game world on the other. Your 600×600 D-pad constraint may evolve significantly.</div></div></body></html>"},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"insight","subtitle":"Your team's next hardware target is taking shape","timestamp":"2026-03-20T02:36:17Z","title":"Meta's dual-display glasses ship this year","type":"html-webview"}
{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_64de6c49bb2eb9b42a3e07f8d00ab768","createdAt":"2026-03-20T02:36:17Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-22T02:36:17Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_bd6fb7882fbddb18fe50d7a2e9921704","message":"Three focused checks to confirm the capture-phase fix actually works on the glasses.","metadata":{"height":330,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;padding:20px;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}h4{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 4px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3}.subtitle{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.4}.msg{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 14px;line-height:1.4}.divider{border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:0}.item{padding:12px 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.4}.item strong{font-weight:600}.item-desc{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:2px 0 0}</style></head><body><h4>MRBD: what to test after the D-pad patch</h4><div class='subtitle'>You fixed 39 files — here's how to verify on-device</div><p class='msg'>Three focused checks to confirm the capture-phase fix actually works on the glasses.</p><hr class='divider'><div class='item'><strong>Open keytest.html on the glasses first</strong><div class='item-desc'>Verify the page logs ArrowUp/Down/Left/Right and Enter with the expected key values. If they show up correctly, the capture-phase approach is working.</div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='item'><strong>Test a game with rapid directional input</strong><div class='item-desc'>Pick Dungeon Crawl or Snake — both need fast arrow-key sequences. Check for dropped inputs or accidental focus shifts when pressing directions quickly.</div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='item'><strong>Confirm Enter triggers actions, not focus clicks</strong><div class='item-desc'>In any game with a start screen, verify that Enter/pinch starts the game rather than clicking a random focused element. The tabindex=\"0\" on body should keep focus anchored.</div></div></body></html>"},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"suggestions","subtitle":"You fixed 39 files — here's how to verify on-device","timestamp":"2026-03-20T02:36:17Z","title":"MRBD: what to test after the D-pad patch","type":"html-webview"}
