{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_3499b675ea28cbd97d56d82fa30f46b2","createdAt":"2026-03-20T02:36:17Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-22T02:36:17Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_7d0fd691667d098204c852e22e5eb1c5","message":"At the world's largest assistive tech conference, Aira announced a partnership with Meta — bringing visual interpretation services to Ray-Ban Meta glasses for the blind community.","metadata":{"height":380,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}a.card-link{display:block;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}a.card-link:active{opacity:0.7}.hero-img{width:100%;height:clamp(120px,34vw,220px);object-fit:cover;display:block;background:var(--border)}.content{padding:16px 20px 20px}.headline{font-size:18px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--text)}.source{font-size:13px;color:var(--tertiary);font-weight:500;margin:0 0 10px}.summary{font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55;margin:0}</style></head><body><a class='card-link' href='https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZOWygi3jrkw' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'><img class='hero-img' src='https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574717025058-2f8737d2e2b7?w=800&h=400&fit=crop' alt='Smart glasses accessibility' onerror=\"this.style.display='none'\"><div class='content'><div class='headline'>CSUN 2026: Aira Partners with Meta on Accessibility</div><div class='source'>Double Tap · Mar 15, 2026</div><div class='summary'>At the 41st CSUN Assistive Technology Conference in Anaheim, Aira announced a partnership with Meta to bring visual interpretation services to Ray-Ban Meta smart glasses. The collaboration lets blind and low-vision users connect with trained Aira agents through the glasses' camera and speaker — no phone required. Other highlights included Orbit Research's new Braille displays and the Vision Ergo magnifier. Directly relevant to the wearables platform you're building on.</div></div></a></body></html>","web_images":[{"image_url":"https://www.youtube.com/img/desktop/yt_1200.png","source_url":"https://youtube.com/watch"}]},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"articles","subtitle":"Double Tap · Mar 15, 2026","timestamp":"2026-03-20T02:36:17Z","title":"CSUN 2026: Aira Partners with Meta on Accessibility","type":"html-webview"}
